1
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:53,970
<i>Chiara.</i>

2
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:55,889
<i>What are you doing?</i>

3
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:57,682
<i>And where are you going?</i>

4
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,604
Didn't I already tell you?

5
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:03,730
I don't want this anymore!

6
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:07,984
Then why are you forcing this on me?

7
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,530
Isn't there a better way?

8
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:16,576
You can't escape what's already
been destined for you, my child.

9
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:23,917
We have reason to believe

10
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,961
that all this time, the Concordat
has never stopped keeping an eye on you.

11
00:01:28,254 --> 00:01:30,215
Then we need to do everything
we can to get her back.

12
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:33,468
- It's not that easy?
- You don't understand.

13
00:01:33,551 --> 00:01:34,969
You owe me.

14
00:01:35,053 --> 00:01:37,055
For all the sacrifices I've made.
Now I'm coming to collect.

15
00:01:37,138 --> 00:01:40,642
The person who I love needs my help.

16
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:46,064
- Whose could this be?
- Someone from outside!

17
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:48,483
Come on, let's find out.

18
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,904
Ma'am. Sorry to bother you.

19
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:54,489
We found a motorcycle outside.

20
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:56,991
Looks like we may have
an unauthorized visitor.

21
00:02:01,454 --> 00:02:03,998
Mom. I'm going to look for Dad.

22
00:02:04,082 --> 00:02:05,708
You just need to keep yourself safe.

23
00:02:06,417 --> 00:02:07,836
Mom, please just listen to me.

24
00:02:07,919 --> 00:02:10,380
I'll explain everything, okay?

25
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:16,344
Captain Pepe, please go to my mom.

26
00:02:16,427 --> 00:02:18,638
- Please take care of her.
- Okay, Mikoy.

27
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:19,931
- We'll take care of it.
- Thank you.

28
00:02:20,014 --> 00:02:21,558
Okay, we'll leave you now.

29
00:02:21,641 --> 00:02:23,226
Mikoy, is your dad Mario missing?

30
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:26,563
You know him.

31
00:02:27,063 --> 00:02:28,273
Maybe he's just being proactive.

32
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:30,608
He's looking for Chiara on his own.

33
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:35,572
So your dad does have
a highly effective habit after all.

34
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,077
I have a hunch.

35
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,539
- You do?
- What hunch?

36
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:47,542
I think Mario knows something.

37
00:02:48,126 --> 00:02:50,712
He may have seen something
or followed someone.

38
00:03:17,155 --> 00:03:18,448
Mario?

39
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:20,783
Rahmboy?

40
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:24,954
- Rahmboy.
- That's right.

41
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:26,039
- Mario.
- But why…?

42
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:32,253
I'm just following orders.

43
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:36,341
Rahmboy.

44
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:52,023
Why didn't he tell me?

45
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:56,903
That's what I'm worried about too.

46
00:03:57,946 --> 00:04:00,031
But he's trying to protect you, Mikoy.

47
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:02,951
He's trying to be a good father to you.

48
00:04:05,703 --> 00:04:07,205
So what do we do now?

49
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:11,918
Call Dara and check Mario's phone.

50
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:14,420
Let's see if my hunch is right.

51
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:31,020
Sean has been talking
to someone suspicious.

52
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:36,609
There's a new character
in Chiara and Mikoy's lives.

53
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:46,703
And now she's a runaway bride?

54
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:08,599
We need to investigate this Vicky.

55
00:05:29,829 --> 00:05:30,830
Vicky?

56
00:05:33,916 --> 00:05:35,335
What does this mean?

57
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:38,755
Rahmboy?

58
00:05:40,214 --> 00:05:41,299
What is this?

59
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:45,178
Have you lost your touch, Isidro?

60
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:50,183
Don't you realize
the predicament you are in?

61
00:05:53,311 --> 00:05:55,396
You're the one who took Chiara.

62
00:05:56,105 --> 00:05:58,733
Technically, I didn't take her.

63
00:05:58,816 --> 00:06:00,443
She came with me willingly.

64
00:06:00,943 --> 00:06:03,529
What do you have on her
that makes her obey you?

65
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:08,242
Chiara came with me because she wanted to.

66
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:11,370
She doesn't want to marry
Mikoy anymore, your son.

67
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:13,122
Is that so hard to understand?

68
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:16,167
Maybe Mikoy did something to her.

69
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:18,377
Or maybe Chiara finally realized

70
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:22,131
that she doesn't really want
the life in Albay.

71
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:27,386
You clearly don't understand
the concept of love.

72
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:31,224
The love between those two
isn't that shallow.

73
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:34,227
I don't think so either.

74
00:06:34,852 --> 00:06:37,480
There's someone more suitable for Chiara,

75
00:06:37,563 --> 00:06:39,398
and it's not Mikoy.

76
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:47,698
And who gave you the right
to choose for Chiara?

77
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:49,200
She has parents.

78
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:50,701
Viktor and Donabel.

79
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:58,167
Being a mother isn't about blood.

80
00:06:59,710 --> 00:07:02,463
I'm the one who raised her.
I'm the one who sacrificed.

81
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:03,881
So I have every right.

82
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:07,218
Besides,

83
00:07:09,303 --> 00:07:10,513
you're the reason

84
00:07:10,596 --> 00:07:13,224
why I lost my family.

85
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:15,768
Spare me the lecture,

86
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:18,938
Mr. Butuan Executioner.

87
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:28,072
You've been enjoying
your role a little too much

88
00:07:28,156 --> 00:07:29,490
as a family man.

89
00:07:30,074 --> 00:07:33,870
You've forgotten what you did
when you were still an executioner.

90
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:42,378
<i>My family lived a quiet life.</i>

91
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,172
<i>A simple life.</i>

92
00:07:44,755 --> 00:07:46,132
<i>Simple dreams.</i>

93
00:07:47,091 --> 00:07:48,759
<i>Simple joys.</i>

94
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:52,513
<i>But because we were poor,</i>

95
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:57,393
<i>we were mercilessly victimized</i>
<i>by those in power.</i>

96
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:05,234
<i>That's why I swore to myself</i>

97
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:08,446
<i>that I would make</i>
<i>anyone who oppressed us pay.</i>

98
00:08:09,197 --> 00:08:10,573
<i>And your group was one of them.</i>

99
00:08:11,157 --> 00:08:12,366
<i>Isidro Catacutan.</i>

100
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:16,162
<i>The man who ruined my life.</i>

101
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:19,582
<i>Revenge isn't easy.</i>

102
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,794
<i>Seeking justice isn't easy either.</i>

103
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:40,978
<i>You need power to make everyone feel</i>

104
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:45,650
<i>how painful it is to have</i>
<i>a mother's heart shattered.</i>

105
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:52,698
I promise you,

106
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:56,619
I'll make whoever did this to you pay.

107
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:20,685
That was an operation created
to liberate the people

108
00:09:20,768 --> 00:09:22,103
of Sitio Bungkal.

109
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:31,112
An authorized operation,
yet my family got caught in it.

110
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:33,739
Was killing them authorized too?

111
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:36,117
They were innocent.

112
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:41,163
The very people who are supposed
to protect the innocent

113
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:43,416
are often the ones who kill them.

114
00:09:44,917 --> 00:09:46,586
Is that what you swore to do?

115
00:09:52,508 --> 00:09:54,260
I fought the case.

116
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:56,762
I went everywhere.

117
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:02,602
Isidro Catacutan.

118
00:10:03,894 --> 00:10:06,272
The Butuan Executioner.

119
00:10:08,399 --> 00:10:11,611
But then I found out
that you were supposedly dead.

120
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:17,742
I thought that weeds don't die so easily.

121
00:10:25,124 --> 00:10:26,917
But what could I do?

122
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:28,127
You were supposedly dead.

123
00:10:28,669 --> 00:10:32,423
So instead of seeking justice,

124
00:10:32,506 --> 00:10:35,217
I went abroad.

125
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:38,095
Little did I know you were just here.

126
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:39,597
Alive and well.

127
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:42,141
With a family. Happy.

128
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:47,480
While I had to settle for loving people
who weren't even related to me.

129
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,571
Vicky.

130
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:59,241
I know that no matter what I say,

131
00:11:00,576 --> 00:11:03,496
it won't lessen the pain
you're feeling right now.

132
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:09,502
I'm a parent too.

133
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:14,340
One wrong

134
00:11:15,841 --> 00:11:17,385
doesn't make another wrong right.

135
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:23,224
You have no right to tell me
what's right and wrong.

136
00:11:23,307 --> 00:11:25,226
You killed my family.

137
00:11:25,309 --> 00:11:26,977
So you should die too.

138
00:12:12,314 --> 00:12:14,150
Dara said that they already found
Sir Mario's location,

139
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:15,818
and they will send coordinates.

140
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:24,285
Hello? Mikoy. Sorry, it took a while,

141
00:12:24,368 --> 00:12:26,287
but they were able to trace
Sir Mario's location.

142
00:12:53,731 --> 00:12:55,357
I'm going to do what's right.

143
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:03,616
What are you doing here?

144
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:07,495
Do you hold a grudge against me?

145
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:08,662
No, Uncle Mario.

146
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:11,999
I just owe her a debt of gratitude,
that's why I follow her.

147
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:17,046
But I can't bear to see you die.

148
00:13:17,671 --> 00:13:19,340
You and Aunt Tess have been good to me,

149
00:13:19,423 --> 00:13:21,300
so I'm here to help you.

150
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:24,678
Thank you.

151
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:28,265
Mario.

152
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:29,850
The car keys.

153
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:34,855
Go through the back.
I'm sure no one's guarding it.

154
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:36,982
Thank you.

155
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:38,692
Aren't you coming with me?

156
00:13:38,776 --> 00:13:40,736
I still have something to do here.

157
00:13:40,819 --> 00:13:42,863
I need to take Chiara with me.

158
00:13:45,115 --> 00:13:46,450
That's what I won't allow.

159
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:49,495
Mario, leave now before I change my mind.

160
00:14:15,479 --> 00:14:16,772
Chiara!

161
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:19,358
- Chiara!
- What happened?

162
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:21,318
Rio has already sent someone to kill you.

163
00:14:21,402 --> 00:14:22,778
You have to obey him now!

164
00:14:24,905 --> 00:14:27,324
There isn't much.
There are only a few of them.

165
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:29,368
Kill Rio.

166
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:31,579
So you and Mikoy can finally be free.

167
00:14:35,916 --> 00:14:37,501
I'll take care of him.

168
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:36,787
Who sent you?!

169
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,542
Dad Mario.

170
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:58,600
Dad Mario!

171
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:00,227
Dad…

172
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:03,522
- Dad Mario.
- Chiara.

173
00:17:03,605 --> 00:17:05,607
This shouldn't have happened to Dad Mario.

174
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:06,859
I'll get help.

175
00:17:06,942 --> 00:17:08,235
- Listen to me.
- No.

176
00:17:08,318 --> 00:17:09,486
No.

177
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:11,155
Hang on, Dad Mario!

178
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:13,490
I'll fix this. I'll get help.

179
00:18:01,371 --> 00:18:03,082
My prayers have been answered.

180
00:18:04,792 --> 00:18:06,794
Heaven is on my side.

181
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:17,971
You've lost.

182
00:19:07,354 --> 00:19:09,690
Looks like we're
getting close to Dad Mario.

183
00:19:09,773 --> 00:19:11,233
But the tracker stopped.

184
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:16,029
So that means Chiara is here too,

185
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:17,489
if he managed to find her.

186
00:19:17,573 --> 00:19:21,910
And if his tracker suddenly stopped,

187
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:24,496
then this place must have a signal jammer.

188
00:19:29,334 --> 00:19:31,461
I've already contacted
the local authorities.

189
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:34,089
I'll just give them
the specific coordinates.

190
00:20:03,702 --> 00:20:04,578
No.

191
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:07,664
You lost.

192
00:20:10,334 --> 00:20:13,086
You haven't won at love yet.

193
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:13,814
Dad Mario, I'm here.

194
00:21:14,439 --> 00:21:15,524
Dad Mario.

195
00:21:17,567 --> 00:21:18,860
Dad Mario.

196
00:21:23,532 --> 00:21:27,160
No, I'm right here, Dad Mario.

197
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:28,620
Dad Mario.

198
00:21:29,246 --> 00:21:30,872
Daddy Mario!

199
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:40,841
I didn't mean to. I didn't mean to.

200
00:21:52,602 --> 00:21:54,062
I didn't know.

201
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:56,189
I didn't know.

202
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:37,773
<i>We need you here.</i>

203
00:22:37,856 --> 00:22:39,649
You need to come here.

204
00:22:45,405 --> 00:22:46,615
Let's go.

205
00:23:52,597 --> 00:23:53,598
Dad.

206
00:23:58,937 --> 00:23:59,896
Dad.

207
00:24:04,901 --> 00:24:05,777
Dad.

208
00:24:08,613 --> 00:24:09,614
Dad.

209
00:24:11,616 --> 00:24:12,701
Dad, why?

210
00:24:15,162 --> 00:24:16,121
Dad.

211
00:24:18,623 --> 00:24:19,666
Dad.

212
00:24:21,376 --> 00:24:22,460
Dad!

213
00:24:27,507 --> 00:24:28,758
Dad…

214
00:24:34,264 --> 00:24:35,265
Dad…

215
00:24:40,812 --> 00:24:41,646
Dad!

216
00:24:49,321 --> 00:24:50,363
Dad.

217
00:24:50,447 --> 00:24:51,531
Dad.

218
00:24:51,615 --> 00:24:52,532
Dad.

219
00:24:54,618 --> 00:24:55,702
Dad!

220
00:24:59,456 --> 00:25:00,332
Dad…

221
00:25:02,792 --> 00:25:04,211
I'm sorry, Dad.

222
00:25:05,712 --> 00:25:06,963
I'm sorry.

223
00:25:48,129 --> 00:25:49,839
This is my promise to you, Dad.

224
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:52,259
I will make those people pay.

225
00:25:54,010 --> 00:25:57,514
The Concordat keeps getting away from us.

226
00:25:57,597 --> 00:25:59,599
Does this agency
even serve a purpose anymore?

227
00:25:59,683 --> 00:26:03,311
You might forgot,
they killed Mario Pinagpala,

228
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:04,646
the father of Mikoy!

229
00:26:09,734 --> 00:26:12,112
I have to accept
the fact that I'm a Valtrovi.

230
00:26:12,195 --> 00:26:15,198
I will die as a true Mafia.

231
00:26:18,118 --> 00:26:21,079
I will send him
to where his father is now.

232
00:26:24,541 --> 00:26:26,251
Don't we have connections in Prague?

233
00:26:26,334 --> 00:26:27,919
Well, yes, but…

234
00:26:28,003 --> 00:26:31,006
with the chance of them
helping us with Chiara's case,

235
00:26:31,089 --> 00:26:32,465
I doubt it very much.

236
00:26:32,549 --> 00:26:34,634
It doesn't matter if you can do
something about it or not.

237
00:26:34,718 --> 00:26:37,846
<i>I made a promise that I will</i>
<i>make those people pay.</i>

238
00:26:37,929 --> 00:26:38,847
And, that's exactly what I'm going to do.
